<BaseLayout title="Corrections" description="Correction route and response SLA for SEO Fan-out." canonicalPath="/korrekturen/" pageClass="reference-page"><header class="reference-hero"><p class="mono-label">Correction policy · owner: Matthias Ramahi</p><h1>Report a problem. Get a dated response.</h1><p>Report factual, methodological, legal, privacy, accessibility or reproducibility problems without confidential or personal data.</p></header><section class="reference-section split-section"><div><h2>Correction SLA</h2><p>Complete reports are acknowledged within five German business days and receive a triage decision within ten. Critical legal, privacy, security or materially false public claims are reviewed within two business days. Accepted standard corrections are published within 30 calendar days or receive a dated status note.</p></div><div><h2>Public route</h2><p>Include the affected URL, observed problem, reproduction steps and a non-confidential source.</p><a class="button-link" href="https://github.com/lia-xim/seo-fanout.com/issues/new">Open correction issue <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></section><section class="reference-section"><div class="section-heading"><p class="mono-label">Closure</p><h2>Every accepted report gets a visible outcome.</h2></div><p>The issue links the fix, explains a rejection, or carries a dated delay note. Silent closure is not the policy.</p></section></BaseLayout>
